From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:47:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PermissionController: Let an app's own request lead over the
 system prompt

When an app targeting API 32 or lower starts, Android opens the
notification prompt for it (REQUEST_PERMISSIONS_FOR_OTHER) as a task
overlay. If the app then asks for permissions itself, the second
GrantPermissionsActivity used to merge into the first as a delegated
follower, and wait paused beneath the overlay until the first finished.
The app's launch transition waits for that second activity to resume, so
on Deckard the launch stalled until the 5 s readiness timeout.

Marathon draws the prompts, so the overlay needn't stay on top. The app's
activity now leads: it takes the system dialog's permissions, including
the system-requested ones, and the system dialog, which needs no result,
finishes. One activity resumes and asks for everything in one flow.
Kept upstream's path when the system dialog already has followers.

Change-Id: If633d56554c43779505f12c62ed35c67565193d7
---
 .../permission/ui/GrantPermissionsActivity.java           | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/PermissionController/src/com/android/permissioncontroller/permission/ui/GrantPermissionsActivity.java b/PermissionController/src/com/android/permissioncontroller/permission/ui/GrantPermissionsActivity.java
index 913f31d..75da0e2 100644
--- a/PermissionController/src/com/android/permissioncontroller/permission/ui/GrantPermissionsActivity.java
+++ b/PermissionController/src/com/android/permissioncontroller/permission/ui/GrantPermissionsActivity.java
@@ -385,6 +385,14 @@ public class GrantPermissionsActivity extends SettingsActivity
                 current.onNewFollowerActivityLocked(null, mRequestedPermissions, false);
                 finishAfterTransition();
                 return;
+            } else if (current.mIsSystemTriggered && current.mFollowerActivities.isEmpty()) {
+                // Deckard: Marathon draws the prompt, so the system's overlay dialog needn't
+                // stay above this one, which would wait paused beneath it. This leads; the
+                // system dialog needs no result.
+                mSystemRequestedPermissions.addAll(current.mSystemRequestedPermissions);
+                sCurrentGrantRequests.put(mKey, this);
+                onNewFollowerActivityLocked(null, current.mRequestedPermissions, false);
+                current.finishAfterTransition();
             } else if (current.mIsSystemTriggered) {
                 // merge into the system triggered dialog, which has task overlay set
                 mDelegated = true;
